    (v_topic_id, 'Patient #65218: What is the most appropriate diagnostic maneuver for a 5-year-old man suspected of having Benign Paroxysmal Positional Vertigo (BPPV) of the posterior semicircular canal?', '["Dix-Hallpike maneuver", "Epley maneuver", "Head thrust test (Halmagyi)", "Romberg test", "Caloric testing"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The Dix-Hallpike maneuver is the diagnostic test for posterior canal BPPV. A positive test elicits vertigo and an upbeat, torsional nystagmus. The Epley maneuver is therapeutic, not diagnostic.'),
