    (v_topic_id, 'Patient #57334: What is the recommended initial lifestyle and dietary modification for a 12-year-old female diagnosed with Meniere''s disease?', '["Low-salt diet and restriction of caffeine/alcohol", "High-protein, low-carbohydrate diet", "Avoiding rapid head turning", "Strict bed rest for 1 week", "Epley maneuver daily"]'::jsonb, 0, 'The initial management of Meniere''s disease (endolymphatic hydrops) focuses on reducing endolymph fluid volume. This is achieved via a low-salt diet and avoiding triggers like caffeine, alcohol, and nicotine. Diuretics (e.g., HCTZ) are added if dietary changes fail.'),
